{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G33VibJA7k367uSBzJpUBN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `picoquic/bytestream.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! A small cursor-over-buffer helper used by `logwriter.c` /\n4\t//! `logreader.c` (binlog) and the connection-id encoding paths.\n5\t//! Three storage modes share a single [`ByteStream`] type:\n6\t//!\n7\t//! * **Borrowed** — wrap a caller-owned slice via\n8\t//!   [`ByteStream::from_slice`].  C: `bytestream_ref_init`.\n9\t//! * **Inline** — a stack-allocated [`ByteStreamBuf`] holds 2560\n10\t//!   bytes of inline storage; [`ByteStreamBuf::stream`] hands out a\n11\t//!   [`ByteStream`] borrowing from it.  C: `bytestream_buf` +\n12\t//!   `bytestream_buf_init`.\n13\t//! * **Owned** — [`ByteStream::with_capacity`] returns a\n14\t//!   `ByteStream<'static>` that owns its heap buffer.  C:\n15\t//!   `bytestream_alloc` + `bytestream_delete` (the latter folds\n16\t//!   into `Drop`).\n17\t//!\n18\t//! ## Shape choices\n19\t//!\n20\t//! C: `bytestream { uint8_t* data; size_t size; size_t ptr; }`.\n21\t//! Rust: `ByteStream<'a> { data: ByteStreamData<'a>, ptr: usize }`.\n22\t//! `data` collapses the C `(uint8_t*, size_t)` pair into one slice\n23\t//! whose `.len()` subsumes `size`; the enum variant distinguishes\n24\t//! borrowed from owned storage so all three constructors produce\n25\t//! the same type.\n26\t//!\n27\t//! C `bytestream_buf { bytestream s; uint8_t buf[2560]; }` aliased\n28\t//! `s.data` against `buf` after init — a self-referential pair.\n29\t//! The Rust shape avoids that: [`ByteStreamBuf`] is just storage,\n30\t//! and [`ByteStreamBuf::stream`] returns a `ByteStream<'_>`\n31\t//! borrowing from the inline buffer for the duration of one I/O\n32\t//! pass.\n33\t//!\n34\t//! Operations are methods on [`ByteStream`].  C `int` 0/-1 returns\n35\t//! become `Result<T, Error>`; out-parameters fold into the `Ok`\n36\t//! variant (e.g., C `int byteread_int8(bytestream*, uint8_t*)`\n37\t//! becomes `fn read_u8(&mut self) -> Result<u8, Error>`).\n38\t//!\n39\t//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only; every body is `todo!()`.\n40\t\n41\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n42\t\n43\tuse crate::ConnectionId;\n44\tuse crate::Error;\n45\t\n46\t/// Inline-buffer capacity carried by [`ByteStreamBuf`].  C:\n47\t/// `BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE`.\n48\tpub const BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE: usize = 2560;\n49\t\n50\t/// Backing storage for a [`ByteStream`].\n51\t///\n52\t/// An enum so that all three C constructors (ref / buf / alloc)\n53\t/// produce a single [`ByteStream`] type rather than splitting into\n54\t/// \"borrowed\" and \"owned\" variants.\n55\tpub enum ByteStreamData<'a> {\n56\t    /// Slice borrowed from external storage — caller-supplied\n57\t    /// buffer ([`ByteStream::from_slice`]) or the inline buffer of\n58\t    /// a [`ByteStreamBuf`] ([`ByteStreamBuf::stream`]).\n59\t    Borrowed(&'a mut [u8]),\n60\t    /// Heap-allocated buffer owned by the bytestream.  Used by\n61\t    /// [`ByteStream::with_capacity`].  Freed by the [`Drop`] impl\n62\t    /// on the vector — replaces the explicit `bytestream_delete`\n63\t    /// call in C.\n64\t    Owned(Vec<u8>),\n65\t}\n66\t\n67\t/// Cursor over a byte buffer.  C: `bytestream`.\n68\t///\n69\t/// The cursor advances monotonically as bytes are read or written.\n70\t/// `data.len()` (under whichever variant) corresponds to the C\n71\t/// `size` field; the cursor offset corresponds to the C `ptr`\n72\t/// field.\n73\t// Phase 1: fields are private (encapsulated) but every method body\n74\t// is `todo!()`, so nothing reads them yet.  The allow drops in\n75\t// Phase 3 once bodies land.\n76\t#[allow(dead_code)]\n77\tpub struct ByteStream<'a> {\n78\t    data: ByteStreamData<'a>,\n79\t    ptr: usize,\n80\t}\n81\t\n82\t/// Inline 2560-byte storage for a stack-allocated bytestream.\n83\t/// C: `bytestream_buf`.\n84\t///\n85\t/// Pair with [`ByteStreamBuf::stream`] to get a usable cursor:\n86\t///\n87\t/// ```ign